        "answer": {
          "short": "10 faces; a solid with two square faces and eight triangular faces.\n\nThe squares lie in parallel planes, with one turned relative to the other; triangles join their vertices.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}8-16+F&=2\\\\F-8&=2\\\\F&=10\\end{align*}$$\n\nUse two squares in parallel planes, with one turned through $45^\\circ$ relative to the other, and join them with eight triangular faces. This gives 10 faces and 8 vertices. The squares contribute 8 edges and the joining triangles contribute 8 further edges, giving 16 edges.",
